Usage: less [OPTION]... [FILE]...

A pager for viewing files, similar to more but with more features.
Allows backward movement in the file as well as forward movement.

Interactive commands include SPACE/f, ENTER/j/e, k/y, b, d/u, g/G, NUMg, NUM%, /, ?, n, N, :n, :p, :f, =, Ctrl-G, r/R, and q.

OPTIONS:
  -e, --quit-at-eof         quit after second EOF
  -E, --QUIT-AT-EOF         quit after first EOF
  -F, --quit-if-one-screen  quit if entire file fits on first screen
  -i, --ignore-case         ignore case in searches that do not contain
                            uppercase
  -I, --IGNORE-CASE         ignore case in all searches
  -K, --quit-on-intr        exit less in response to Ctrl+C
  -n, --line-numbers        display line number at start of each line
  -N, --LINE-NUMBERS        display line number at start of each line
  -S, --chop-long-lines     chop long lines (do not wrap)
  -q, --quiet               accepted placeholder; terminal bell is not used
  -Q, --QUIET               accepted placeholder; terminal bell is not used
  -r, --raw-control-chars   accepted placeholder; control chars are passed
                            through
  -R, --RAW-CONTROL-CHARS   accepted placeholder; ANSI SGR color sequences are
                            passed through
      --no-init             accepted placeholder; terminal init/deinit sequences
                            are not used
  -z, --window NUM          set scrolling window size
  -NUM                      same as -z NUM
      --help                display this help and exit
  -V, --version             output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
